+# Lane A evidence (streamer reactions) — 2026-11-17
+
+Labels: **SYNTHETIC** = generated by tools/gameplay-eval/make_*.py, built and tuned by the same author.
+**REAL** = real Twitch VOD sample, private, never committed (test-footage/ is git-ignored).
+
+## SYNTHETIC matrix (326 s, 8 scenarios, cartoon facecam, synthetic voices)
+| selector | positives found (of 5) | false picks |
+|---|---|---|
+| V9 audio-peak picker | 3 | 3 |
+| new reaction detector, tuning set (variant 0) | 4 | 0 |
+| new reaction detector, held-out set (variant 1) | 5 | 0 |
+Facecam position was supplied for the synthetic runs (YuNet does not recognise a cartoon face).
+
+## REAL sample (Twitch VOD, Spanish-speaking streamer, GTA V with facecam; 4 x 5 min + 4 min, 360p)
+* Facecam auto-found on the real streamer (after switching to cluster-based selection; the first version failed here).
+* Reaction picks (by the detector): 3 in ~20 min of footage, plus ignored silent game events.
+* Visual check of the facecam frames at 2 picks: arms-up celebration + laugh; face-palm + animated explaining -> both look like real reactions.
+  Transcript of the second: "...estoy completamente loco chavales" (faster-whisper base, Spanish).
+* Observed failure mode: in one pick the audio was GAME cutscene dialogue (English), not the streamer; the pick was still right
+  because the facecam showed a real reaction, but voice-only evidence can be fooled by game dialogue.
+* NOT measured: precision/recall on real footage (no labels), recall of missed reactions, other games/streamers/languages.
+* Timing: 13-23 s per 300 s of video on this laptop CPU path (voice + facecam + frame evidence); memory/VRAM not measured.
